{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: x taken as real on [0, 1] (say \"integer x\" for whole numbers)\n  ucas: it(x: real in 0..1) = x^2\n  ucas: approx it degree 5 keep crit\n  keep crit: no critical points inside [0, 1]\napprox it on [0, 1] as f32, fma\n  checked: it is even (f(-x) = f(x) at 64 points): fitting P(x^2) on [0, 1]\n  metric: relative error\n  no polynomial fit in the degree range\n  rational fits (num/den degree: minimax, Pade; max rel error):\n    2/2 0 (0) 4/2 1.29e-13 (-) 2/4 1.73e-19 (0) 4/4 6.95e-14 (-)\n    2/6 1.45e-19 (0) 4/6 0 (-)\n  piecewise (2 pieces split at 0.5, max rel error): 1: 1 2: 1.08e-19 3: 1.08e-19 4: 1.33e-19 5: 1.26e-19\n  candidates ranked by max ulp and cost under gt1030 (sampled floats); defined as ap1..:\n  measured on 130809 f32 in [0, 1]; ulp against the exact value (naive rounding in parentheses)\n  #   kind      deg   form        error (naive)            max rel       max abs       cost\n  1   piecewise 5     horner+fma  0.988 ulp                1             4.37e-08      17.5 at x=0.504203856\n      2 pieces, of |x|: fma(fma(fma(fma(fma(k5, t, k4), t, k3), t, k2), t, k1), t, k0) where a = abs(x), lo = a < 0.5, t = a - (lo ? f32(0.0) : f32(0.75)), k0 = lo ? f32(0.0) : f32(0.5625), k1 = lo ? f32(0.0) : f32(1.5), k2 = lo ? f32(1.0) : f32(0.99999994), k3 = lo ? f32(0.0) : f32(0.0), k4 = lo ? f32(0.0) : f32(0.0), k5 = lo ? f32(0.0) : f32(7.1075003e-20)\n      rounding of ap1, first order, 6 operations, relative, in u = 2^-24: worst case 5, probable no better (under 16 operations), expected 1.53; `error ap1 ~ F` says what each means\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "approximate x^2 in 0..1 degree 5 crit", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x: real in 0..1) = x^2", "approx it degree 5 keep crit"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "approx", "function": "it", "lo": 0, "hi": 1, "metric": "max ulp",